{"body":[{"type":"section","heading":"Getting started","level":1,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"This article explains how to integrate MDX into your project. It shows how to use MDX with your bundler and JSX runtime of choice. To understand how the MDX format works, we recommend that you start with § What is MDX. See § Using MDX when you’re all set up and ready to use MDX."},{"type":"section","heading":"Contents","level":2,"body":[{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":["Prerequisites"]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":["Bundler","JSX","Editor","Types","Security"]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":["Bundlers","Build systems","Compilers","Site generators","JSX runtimes","JavaScript engines"]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":["Further reading"]}]},{"type":"section","heading":"Prerequisites","level":2,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"MDX relies on JSX, so it’s required that your project supports JSX as well. Any JSX runtime (React, Preact, Vue, etc.) will do. Note that we do compile JSX to JavaScript for you so you don’t have to set that up."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"All @mdx-js/* packages are written in modern JavaScript. A Node.js version of 16 or later is needed to use them. Our packages are also ESM only."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Note: Using Rust instead of Node.js? Try mdxjs-rs!"}]},{"type":"section","heading":"Quick start","level":2,"body":[{"type":"section","heading":"Bundler","level":3,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"MDX is a language that’s compiled to JavaScript. (We also compile regular markdown to JavaScript.) The easiest way to get started is to use an integration for your bundler if you have one:"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":["if you use esbuild (or Bun), install and configure @mdx-js/esbuild","if you use Rollup (or Vite), install and configure @mdx-js/rollup","if you use webpack (or Next.js), install and configure @mdx-js/loader"]},{"type":"paragraph","text":"You can also use MDX without bundlers:"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":["you can import MDX files in Node.js with @mdx-js/node-loader","you can use our core compiler @mdx-js/mdx to compile MDX files","you can use our core compiler @mdx-js/mdx to evaluate (compile and run) MDX files"]},{"type":"paragraph","text":"For more info on these tools, see their dedicated sections: ¶ Next.js, ¶ Node.js, ¶ Rollup, ¶ Vite, ¶ esbuild, and ¶ webpack."}]},{"type":"section","heading":"JSX","level":3,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Now you’ve set up an integration or @mdx-js/mdx itself, it’s time to configure your JSX runtime."},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":["if you use React, that’s the default; optionally install and configure @mdx-js/react","if you use Preact, set jsxImportSource in ProcessorOptions to 'preact'; optionally install and configure @mdx-js/preact","if you use Svelte, install svelte-jsx, and set jsxImportSource in ProcessorOptions to 'svelte-jsx'","if you use Vue, set jsxImportSource in ProcessorOptions to 'vue'; optionally install and configure @mdx-js/vue","if you use Solid, set jsxImportSource in ProcessorOptions to 'solid-js/h'","if you use Emotion, set jsxImportSource in ProcessorOptions to '@emotion/react'","if you use Theme UI, install and configure @mdx-js/react, then wrap your MDX content in a ``"]},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Other JSX runtimes are supported by setting jsxImportSource in ProcessorOptions."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"For more info on these tools, see their dedicated sections: ¶ Emotion, ¶ Preact, ¶ React, ¶ Solid, ¶ Svelte, ¶ Theme UI, and ¶ Vue."}]},{"type":"section","heading":"Editor","level":3,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"You can enhance the experience of using MDX by adding support of it to your editor:"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":["if you use VS Code, try mdx-js/mdx-analyzer","if you use Vim, try jxnblk/vim-mdx-js","if you use Sublime Text, try jonsuh/mdx-sublime","if you use JetBrains IntelliJ/WebStorm, try JetBrains/mdx-intellij-plugin"]},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The syntax highlighting that powers our VS Code extension and that is used to highlight code blocks on GitHub is maintained at wooorm/markdown-tm-language."}]},{"type":"section","heading":"Types","level":3,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"First install the package:"},{"type":"code","text":"npm install @types/mdx","language":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"…TypeScript should automatically pick it up:"},{"type":"code","text":"// @filename: types.d.ts
