// @filename: example.js
// ---cut---
import Post from './post.mdx' // `Post` is now typed.","language":"js twoslash path="example.js""},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Our packages are typed with TypeScript. For types to work, the JSX namespace must be typed. This is done by installing and using the types of your framework, such as @types/react, then augmenting the mdx/types.js module."},{"type":"code","text":"import * as React from "react";

declare module "mdx/types.js" {
  export import JSX = React.JSX;
}","language":"ts twoslash path="example.ts""},{"type":"paragraph","text":"To enable types for imported .mdx, .md, etc., install and use @types/mdx. This package also exports several useful types, such as MDXComponents which represents the components prop. You can import them like so:"},{"type":"code","text":"import type { MDXComponents } from "mdx/types.js";","language":"ts twoslash path="example.ts""}]},{"type":"section","heading":"Security","level":3,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"MDX is a programming language. If you trust your authors, that’s fine. If you don’t, it’s unsafe."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Do not let random people from the internet write MDX. If you do, you might want to look into using <iframe>s with sandbox, but security is hard, and that doesn’t seem to be 100%. For Node.js, vm2 sounds interesting. But you should probably also sandbox the whole OS using Docker or similar, perform rate limiting, and make sure processes can be killed when taking too long."}]}]},{"type":"section","heading":"Integrations","level":2,"body":[{"type":"section","heading":"Bundlers","level":3,"body":[{"type":"section","heading":"esbuild","level":4,"body":[{"type":"code","text":"import mdx from "@mdx-js/esbuild";
